Upstream projects
-----------------

1. bloodborne_pc by Supermedo (https://github.com/Supermedo/bloodborne_pc)
   License: GPL-2.0-or-later
   The native Windows port of Bloodborne. The runtime in src/, the graphics
   shim in gpu/shim/ and parts of the vendored game runtime in gpu/shadps4/
   were taken from this project and adapted for Driveclub. Supermedo's
   project is itself built on the native Linux port by deadinside28 (see
   below).

2. bloodborne_pc by deadinside28 (https://github.com/deadinside28/bloodborne_pc)
   License: GPL-2.0-or-later
   The original native Linux port of Bloodborne, also known as bbport. It is
   the origin of the "bbport:" markers that are in the code of this
   repository and of the vendored shadPS4 tree in gpu/shadps4/.

3. shadPS4 (https://github.com/shadps4-emu/shadPS4)
   License: GPL-2.0-or-later
   The emulator whose video core and shader translator were the starting point
   of the renderer in gpu/shadps4/. That tree is vendored, see gpu/VENDOR.txt.
   The vendored copy also carries the "bbport:" changes of the two projects
   above.

4. shadp2p by Wozzardman (https://github.com/Wozzardman/shadp2p)
   License: GPL-2.0-or-later
   The shadNet client. gpu/shim/core/bloodborne_re.h is the header from
   shadp2p, and the network and NP libraries in gpu/shadps4/core/libraries/
   {network,np} and gpu/bbnet/ come from the shadNet work that was put
   together for bloodborne_pc.

5. BloodBorneButPc by Awaken (https://github.com/Awakenchan/BloodBorneButPc)
   License: GPL-2.0-or-later
   The online play code of the bloodborne_pc projects. The network, NP and
   shadNet glue in gpu/bbnet/ and the matching parts of the vendored tree
   descend from it.

How the reused code can be identified
-------------------------------------

The following in this repository comes from the projects named above:

- The files gpu/shim/bbport_*.c, gpu/shim/bbport_*.h and
  gpu/shim/core/bloodborne_re.h keep the file names of the upstream project.
- 221 comments in gpu/shadps4/ and 27 in gpu/shim/ carry the "bbport:" prefix
  that marks a change made in the upstream bloodborne_pc projects.
  gpu/VENDOR.txt described them as local changes; they are not, they come
  from the two bloodborne_pc projects named above. The changes made for this
  project are marked with "driveclub:" instead, in 95 comments.
- 5 of the 30 files in src/ (compat_win.c, compat_win.h, runtime_ajm.c,
  runtime_rtc.c, vulkan_smoke.c) and 29 of the 50 files in gpu/shim/ are byte
  for byte the same as in Supermedo's bloodborne_pc at commit de2e38a. Two
  files in src/ (runtime_ajm.c, vulkan_smoke.c) and four in gpu/shim/
  (core/address_space.h, core/devtools/widget/gpu_memory.h, tracy/Tracy.hpp,
  tracy/TracyVulkan.hpp) are also the same as in deadinside28's
  bloodborne_pc.
- 216 of the 481 C++ files in gpu/shadps4/ are byte for byte the same as in
  Supermedo's bloodborne_pc at commit de2e38a. 307 of the 481 are byte for
  byte the same as in shadPS4 at commit b4e7ae7. 147 are the same as in no
  commit of either upstream; those are the files that were changed for this
  project.
- gpu/VENDOR.txt was byte for byte the same as in Supermedo's bloodborne_pc
  at commit bf95396.
- The LICENSE file is byte for byte the same as in both bloodborne_pc
  projects.
- The files that were changed for this project carry a notice at the top
  that names the project they are based on; 182 files carry one. The files
  that were taken over unchanged keep their original contents.

Changes made here
-----------------

The Driveclub specific work is: the launcher (launcher/), the patch set in
patches/DriveClub.xml, the runtime adjustments in src/, the graphics changes
in gpu/shim/ and the changes in the vendored renderer. The changes to the
reused files are marked in the source and in the notice at the top of the
changed file.

Third-party components that keep their own license are listed in
packaging/release/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt and have their license file next to
them in the tree.
